-- State Pension Credit Act 2002 -- LAYER 1 TESTS.
--
-- Every expected value in this file was worked out BY HAND from the text of the Act (the
-- working is in the comment above each case) before the file was run, and was never edited to
-- match what the rules printed. A failing assertion here is a finding; NOTES.md reports each
-- one (none was left failing at the time of writing: see NOTES.md, "What check.sh prints").
--
-- Every person, date and figure below is INVENTED. The Act states no amount, percentage or
-- threshold (regulations do), and borrows "pensionable age" from the Pensions Act 1995; the
-- tests supply round figures (P0) and per-person pensionable-age days as plain facts.
--
-- WHAT IS COVERED. Sections 1 to 5 and 3ZA: every branch, with the two sides of the
-- appropriate minimum guarantee, the savings credit threshold, amount A against amount B, 6
-- April 2016, the 65th birthday, the qualifying age day and the section 4(3) minimum. Sections
-- 6 to 10: each rule, with the boundary days. Section 12 and 18A: not-covered answers, asserted.
-- Schedules 1 and 2: each encoded paragraph. Interpretation (15 to 17), the dates, and the
-- Royal Assent date (NOTHING), asserted.

§ `Fixtures`

§§ `The day tested, and the people`

-- All people, dates and figures in these tests are INVENTED to exercise the rules.
-- In particular the two "pensionable age" days in each Person are facts the Act borrows
-- from the Pensions Act 1995 (Schedule 4); they are not worked out from a date of
-- birth here, and no table of pensionable ages is asserted.
GIVETH A DATE
`test day` MEANS YearMonthDay 2026 10 22

-- W1: a woman born 10 May 1950, attains pensionable age 10 May 2010 (so her 65th birthday is 10 May 2015).
GIVETH A Person
`woman W1` MEANS
    Person WITH
        sex IS Woman
        `date of birth` IS YearMonthDay 1950 5 10
        `day pensionable age is attained` IS YearMonthDay 2010 5 10
        `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS YearMonthDay 2010 5 10

-- W2: a woman born 3 March 1952, attains pensionable age 3 March 2012; 65th birthday 3 March 2017.
GIVETH A Person
`woman W2` MEANS
    Person WITH
        sex IS Woman
        `date of birth` IS YearMonthDay 1952 3 3
        `day pensionable age is attained` IS YearMonthDay 2012 3 3
        `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS YearMonthDay 2012 3 3

-- W3: a woman born 1 January 1959, attains pensionable age 1 January 2019 (NOT before 6 April 2016); 65th birthday 1 January 2024.
GIVETH A Person
`woman W3` MEANS
    Person WITH
        sex IS Woman
        `date of birth` IS YearMonthDay 1959 1 1
        `day pensionable age is attained` IS YearMonthDay 2019 1 1
        `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS YearMonthDay 2019 1 1

-- W4: a woman born 1 January 1969, attains pensionable age 1 January 2030, which is after the test day.
GIVETH A Person
`woman W4` MEANS
    Person WITH
        sex IS Woman
        `date of birth` IS YearMonthDay 1969 1 1
        `day pensionable age is attained` IS YearMonthDay 2030 1 1
        `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS YearMonthDay 2030 1 1

-- M1: a man born 10 May 1950. His own pensionable age is 10 May 2015; a woman born the same day attained hers on 10 May 2010, which is his qualifying age (section 1(6)(b)).
GIVETH A Person
`man M1` MEANS
    Person WITH
        sex IS Man
        `date of birth` IS YearMonthDay 1950 5 10
        `day pensionable age is attained` IS YearMonthDay 2015 5 10
        `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS YearMonthDay 2010 5 10

-- E1: attains pensionable age on 5 April 2016, the day BEFORE 6 April 2016; born 5 April 1951 so 65 on 5 April 2016.
GIVETH A Person
`woman E1` MEANS
    Person WITH
        sex IS Woman
        `date of birth` IS YearMonthDay 1951 4 5
        `day pensionable age is attained` IS YearMonthDay 2016 4 5
        `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS YearMonthDay 2016 4 5

-- E2: attains pensionable age on 6 April 2016, which is NOT before 6 April 2016; born 6 April 1951 so 65 on 6 April 2016.
GIVETH A Person
`woman E2` MEANS
    Person WITH
        sex IS Woman
        `date of birth` IS YearMonthDay 1951 4 6
        `day pensionable age is attained` IS YearMonthDay 2016 4 6
        `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS YearMonthDay 2016 4 6

-- B1: a woman born 1 December 1950, pensionable age 1 December 2010, 65th birthday 1 December 2015.
GIVETH A Person
`woman B1` MEANS
    Person WITH
        sex IS Woman
        `date of birth` IS YearMonthDay 1950 12 1
        `day pensionable age is attained` IS YearMonthDay 2010 12 1
        `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age` IS YearMonthDay 2010 12 1

§§ `Income`

GIVETH AN Income
`no income` MEANS
    Income WITH
        earnings IS 0
        `working tax credit` IS 0
        `retirement pension income` IS 0
        `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS 0
        `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS 0
        `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS 0
        `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS 0
        `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS 0
        `income from capital` IS 0
        `income of a prescribed description` IS 0

GIVEN pension IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Income
`a pension income of` pension MEANS
    Income WITH
        earnings IS 0
        `working tax credit` IS 0
        `retirement pension income` IS pension
        `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS 0
        `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS 0
        `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS 0
        `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS 0
        `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS 0
        `income from capital` IS 0
        `income of a prescribed description` IS 0

§§ `Households`

-- Not married, not living together as a couple.
GIVETH A Household
`a single person` MEANS
    Household WITH
        `married to or civil partners of each other` IS FALSE
        `members of the same household` IS FALSE
        `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS FALSE
        `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS FALSE

-- Married or civil partners, members of the same household: a couple under limb (a).
GIVETH A Household
`a married couple in one household` MEANS
    Household WITH
        `married to or civil partners of each other` IS TRUE
        `members of the same household` IS TRUE
        `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS FALSE
        `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS FALSE

-- Not married, living together as a married couple, no prescribed circumstances: a couple under limb (b).
GIVETH A Household
`an unmarried couple living together` MEANS
    Household WITH
        `married to or civil partners of each other` IS FALSE
        `members of the same household` IS FALSE
        `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS TRUE
        `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS FALSE

-- Limb (b) but regulations take them outside it: not a couple.
GIVETH A Household
`an unmarried couple living together in prescribed circumstances` MEANS
    Household WITH
        `married to or civil partners of each other` IS FALSE
        `members of the same household` IS FALSE
        `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS TRUE
        `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS TRUE

-- Married but not members of the same household and not 'living together': not a couple.
GIVETH A Household
`a married pair in different households` MEANS
    Household WITH
        `married to or civil partners of each other` IS TRUE
        `members of the same household` IS FALSE
        `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS FALSE
        `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS FALSE

-- Married, not in the same household for the Act's purposes, yet 'living together': limb (a) fails on household and limb (b) needs them NOT married, so not a couple.
GIVETH A Household
`a married pair in different households who live together` MEANS
    Household WITH
        `married to or civil partners of each other` IS TRUE
        `members of the same household` IS FALSE
        `living together as a married couple or as civil partners` IS TRUE
        `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)` IS FALSE

§§ `Prescribed figures (INVENTED round numbers; the Act states none)`

-- Units are whole pounds a week, as the regulations count; the Act names neither.
-- P0: standard minimum guarantee 300 for a couple and 200 for one person; severe
-- disability adds 50; the section 70 allowance adds 40; threshold 150; amount A is
-- 50 per cent of the excess of qualifying income over the threshold; amount B is 50 per
-- cent of income over the appropriate minimum guarantee; the maximum savings credit is
-- 60 per cent of (standard minimum guarantee less threshold); nothing is payable under 1.

-- P0: the base figures.
GIVETH A Prescribed
`P0` MEANS
    Prescribed WITH
        `standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple` IS 300
        `standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple` IS 200
        `additional amount for a claimant who is severely disabled` IS 50
        `additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` IS 40
        `other prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` IS 0
        `prescribed amount substituted for the standard minimum guarantee` IS NOTHING
        `savings credit threshold` IS 150
        `prescribed percentage for amount A` IS 50
        `prescribed percentage for amount B` IS 50
        `prescribed percentage for the maximum savings credit` IS 60
        `prescribed higher amount substituted for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` IS NOTHING
        `prescribed amount below which state pension credit is not payable` IS 1

-- Same as P0 but nothing below 50 is payable (section 4(3)).
GIVETH A Prescribed
`P0 with a minimum payable of 50` MEANS
    Prescribed WITH
        `standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple` IS 300
        `standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple` IS 200
        `additional amount for a claimant who is severely disabled` IS 50
        `additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` IS 40
        `other prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` IS 0
        `prescribed amount substituted for the standard minimum guarantee` IS NOTHING
        `savings credit threshold` IS 150
        `prescribed percentage for amount A` IS 50
        `prescribed percentage for amount B` IS 50
        `prescribed percentage for the maximum savings credit` IS 60
        `prescribed higher amount substituted for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` IS NOTHING
        `prescribed amount below which state pension credit is not payable` IS 50

-- Section 2(6): in this case 250 replaces the standard minimum guarantee in section 2(3)(a).
GIVETH A Prescribed
`P0 with 250 substituted for the standard minimum guarantee` MEANS
    Prescribed WITH
        `standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple` IS 300
        `standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple` IS 200
        `additional amount for a claimant who is severely disabled` IS 50
        `additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` IS 40
        `other prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` IS 0
        `prescribed amount substituted for the standard minimum guarantee` IS JUST 250
        `savings credit threshold` IS 150
        `prescribed percentage for amount A` IS 50
        `prescribed percentage for amount B` IS 50
        `prescribed percentage for the maximum savings credit` IS 60
        `prescribed higher amount substituted for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` IS NOTHING
        `prescribed amount below which state pension credit is not payable` IS 1

-- Sections 2(6) and 3(5) both in play.
GIVETH A Prescribed
`P0 with 250 substituted and 270 as the higher amount in amount B` MEANS
    Prescribed WITH
        `standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple` IS 300
        `standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple` IS 200
        `additional amount for a claimant who is severely disabled` IS 50
        `additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` IS 40
        `other prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` IS 0
        `prescribed amount substituted for the standard minimum guarantee` IS JUST 250
        `savings credit threshold` IS 150
        `prescribed percentage for amount A` IS 50
        `prescribed percentage for amount B` IS 50
        `prescribed percentage for the maximum savings credit` IS 60
        `prescribed higher amount substituted for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` IS JUST 270
        `prescribed amount below which state pension credit is not payable` IS 1

-- Section 3(5) figure exists but no section 2(6) substitution: the higher amount must NOT be used.
GIVETH A Prescribed
`P0 with only a higher amount of 270 and no substitution` MEANS
    Prescribed WITH
        `standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple` IS 300
        `standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple` IS 200
        `additional amount for a claimant who is severely disabled` IS 50
        `additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` IS 40
        `other prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` IS 0
        `prescribed amount substituted for the standard minimum guarantee` IS NOTHING
        `savings credit threshold` IS 150
        `prescribed percentage for amount A` IS 50
        `prescribed percentage for amount B` IS 50
        `prescribed percentage for the maximum savings credit` IS 60
        `prescribed higher amount substituted for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` IS JUST 270
        `prescribed amount below which state pension credit is not payable` IS 1

-- Used to put amount A and amount B exactly level.
GIVETH A Prescribed
`P0 with amount B at 100 per cent` MEANS
    Prescribed WITH
        `standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple` IS 300
        `standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple` IS 200
        `additional amount for a claimant who is severely disabled` IS 50
        `additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` IS 40
        `other prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` IS 0
        `prescribed amount substituted for the standard minimum guarantee` IS NOTHING
        `savings credit threshold` IS 150
        `prescribed percentage for amount A` IS 50
        `prescribed percentage for amount B` IS 100
        `prescribed percentage for the maximum savings credit` IS 60
        `prescribed higher amount substituted for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` IS NOTHING
        `prescribed amount below which state pension credit is not payable` IS 1

§ `State pension credit: entitlement and amount (sections 1 to 5 and 3ZA)`

-- Method. Each case is one claimant on one day (the test day, 22 October 2026, unless a
-- case sets another). The expected values below were worked out BY HAND from the Act's
-- formulas and P0, and typed in before any run; where a run disagreed, the disagreement
-- was read against the text (see NOTES.md).  Layout of the working: AMG is the
-- appropriate minimum guarantee (section 2(3)); GC the guarantee credit (2(2)); max SC the
-- maximum savings credit (3(7)); A and B the amounts of 3(4); SC the savings credit (3(3)).

§§ `A single woman: guarantee credit and the savings credit threshold`

-- A0: single woman W1, no income at all. AMG = 200 (the single figure, no additions). Section 2(1)(a) 'has no income' is met; 2(2)(a) the credit is the whole AMG, 200. Qualifying income 0 does not exceed the threshold 150, so no savings credit.
GIVETH A Case
`case A0` MEANS
    Case WITH
        `day tested` IS `test day`
        claimant IS `woman W1`
        `other member of the couple` IS `woman W2`
        household IS `a single person`
        `in Great Britain` IS TRUE
        `temporarily absent from Great Britain and entitlement continued by regulations` IS FALSE
        `income of the claimant` IS `no income`
        `qualifying income of the claimant` IS 0
        `income of the other member` IS `no income`
        `qualifying income of the other member` IS 0
        `prescribed circumstances in which the income of the other member is not aggregated` IS FALSE
        `severely disabled` IS FALSE
        `claimant entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS FALSE
        `other member entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS FALSE
        `other member entitled to state pension credit` IS FALSE
        `regulations under section 3ZA(1) prescribe the claimant's case` IS FALSE
        `regulations under section 3(8) take the maximum savings credit to be nil` IS FALSE
        `excluded by section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 as amended by section 4(2)` IS FALSE
        `prescribed circumstances in which an amount below the prescribed amount is payable` IS FALSE
        `a claim has been made and the Administration Act section 1 conditions are met` IS TRUE
        `entitlement restricted by section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998` IS FALSE
        `husband or wife by a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy` IS FALSE
        `either party to the marriage has a spouse additional to the other party` IS FALSE
        `person, other party and additional spouse members of the same household` IS FALSE
        `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `The Act's answer on whether the conditions for entitlement are met` `case A0` `P0` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `The Act's answer on whether the claimant is entitled to state pension credit` `case A0` `P0` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `s 2(3) -- the appropriate minimum guarantee` `case A0` `P0` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 5 -- the income treated as the claimant's` `case A0` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2(2) -- the guarantee credit to which the claimant is entitled` `case A0` `P0` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 3(3) -- the savings credit to which the claimant is entitled` `case A0` `P0` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 4(3) -- the amount of state pension credit to which the claimant is entitled` `case A0` `P0` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 4(3) -- state pension credit is payable` `case A0` `P0`
#ASSERT `The Act's answer on the amount of state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` `case A0` `P0` EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `The Act's answer on the amount of state pension credit to which the claimant is entitled` `case A0` `P0` EQUALS JUST 200

-- A1: single woman W1, income 150 (all retirement pension), qualifying income 150. 2(1)(b): 150 does not exceed 200. GC = 200 - 150 = 50. QI 150 does NOT exceed the threshold 150 (3(2)(a)), so no savings credit. Total 50.
GIVETH A Case
`case A1` MEANS
    Case WITH
        `day tested` IS `test day`
        claimant IS `woman W1`
        `other member of the couple` IS `woman W2`
        household IS `a single person`
        `in Great Britain` IS TRUE
        `temporarily absent from Great Britain and entitlement continued by regulations` IS FALSE
        `income of the claimant` IS `a pension income of` 150
        `qualifying income of the claimant` IS 150
        `income of the other member` IS `no income`
        `qualifying income of the other member` IS 0
        `prescribed circumstances in which the income of the other member is not aggregated` IS FALSE
        `severely disabled` IS FALSE
        `claimant entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS FALSE
        `other member entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS FALSE
        `other member entitled to state pension credit` IS FALSE
        `regulations under section 3ZA(1) prescribe the claimant's case` IS FALSE
        `regulations under section 3(8) take the maximum savings credit to be nil` IS FALSE
        `excluded by section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 as amended by section 4(2)` IS FALSE
        `prescribed circumstances in which an amount below the prescribed amount is payable` IS FALSE
        `a claim has been made and the Administration Act section 1 conditions are met` IS TRUE
        `entitlement restricted by section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998` IS FALSE
        `husband or wife by a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy` IS FALSE
        `either party to the marriage has a spouse additional to the other party` IS FALSE
        `person, other party and additional spouse members of the same household` IS FALSE
        `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `The Act's answer on whether the conditions for entitlement are met` `case A1` `P0` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `The Act's answer on whether the claimant is entitled to state pension credit` `case A1` `P0` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `s 2(3) -- the appropriate minimum guarantee` `case A1` `P0` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 5 -- the income treated as the claimant's` `case A1` EQUALS 150
#ASSERT `s 5 -- the qualifying income treated as the claimant's` `case A1` EQUALS 150
#ASSERT `s 2(2) -- the guarantee credit to which the claimant is entitled` `case A1` `P0` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 3(3) -- the savings credit to which the claimant is entitled` `case A1` `P0` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 4(3) -- the amount of state pension credit to which the claimant is entitled` `case A1` `P0` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 4(3) -- state pension credit is payable` `case A1` `P0`
#ASSERT `The Act's answer on the amount of state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` `case A1` `P0` EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `The Act's answer on the amount of state pension credit to which the claimant is entitled` `case A1` `P0` EQUALS JUST 50

#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(2) -- the second savings credit condition` `case A1` `P0`)

-- A2: as A1 but income and qualifying income 151, one above the threshold. GC = 49. Max SC = 60% x (200 - 150) = 30. A = smaller of 30 and 50% x (151 - 150) = 0.5, so 0.5. B: 151 does not exceed AMG 200, so B = 0 (3(4)(b)). A exceeds B, so SC = 0.5. Total 49.5.
GIVETH A Case
`case A2` MEANS
    Case WITH
        `day tested` IS `test day`
        claimant IS `woman W1`
        `other member of the couple` IS `woman W2`
        household IS `a single person`
        `in Great Britain` IS TRUE
        `temporarily absent from Great Britain and entitlement continued by regulations` IS FALSE
        `income of the claimant` IS `a pension income of` 151
        `qualifying income of the claimant` IS 151
        `income of the other member` IS `no income`
        `qualifying income of the other member` IS 0
        `prescribed circumstances in which the income of the other member is not aggregated` IS FALSE
        `severely disabled` IS FALSE
        `claimant entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS FALSE
        `other member entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS FALSE
        `other member entitled to state pension credit` IS FALSE
        `regulations under section 3ZA(1) prescribe the claimant's case` IS FALSE
        `regulations under section 3(8) take the maximum savings credit to be nil` IS FALSE
        `excluded by section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 as amended by section 4(2)` IS FALSE
        `prescribed circumstances in which an amount below the prescribed amount is payable` IS FALSE
        `a claim has been made and the Administration Act section 1 conditions are met` IS TRUE
        `entitlement restricted by section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998` IS FALSE
        `husband or wife by a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy` IS FALSE
        `either party to the marriage has a spouse additional to the other party` IS FALSE
        `person, other party and additional spouse members of the same household` IS FALSE
        `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `The Act's answer on whether the conditions for entitlement are met` `case A2` `P0` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `The Act's answer on whether the claimant is entitled to state pension credit` `case A2` `P0` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `s 2(2) -- the guarantee credit to which the claimant is entitled` `case A2` `P0` EQUALS 49
#ASSERT `s 3(3) -- the savings credit to which the claimant is entitled` `case A2` `P0` EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `s 4(3) -- the amount of state pension credit to which the claimant is entitled` `case A2` `P0` EQUALS 49.5
#ASSERT `The Act's answer on the amount of state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` `case A2` `P0` EQUALS JUST 49.5

#ASSERT `s 3(7) -- the maximum savings credit` `case A2` `P0` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 3(4) -- amount A` `case A2` `P0` EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `s 3(4) -- amount B` `case A2` `P0` EQUALS 0
-- A3: income 160, QI 160. GC = 40. A = smaller of 30 and 50% x 10 = 5, so 5. B = 0. SC = 5. Total 45.
GIVETH A Case
`case A3` MEANS
    Case WITH
        `day tested` IS `test day`
