§§ `A single woman: the appropriate minimum guarantee as the line`

-- C1: income exactly equal to the AMG (200), qualifying income 100 (below the threshold). 2(1)(b) says income that 'does not exceed' the AMG, so the condition IS met. GC = 200 - 200 = 0. No savings credit. The claimant is entitled (conditions met) to a guarantee credit of nothing; nothing is payable (0 is less than the prescribed minimum 1, section 4(3)).
GIVETH A Case
`case C1` MEANS
    Case WITH
        `day tested` IS `test day`
        claimant IS `woman W1`
        `other member of the couple` IS `woman W2`
        household IS `a single person`
        `in Great Britain` IS TRUE
        `temporarily absent from Great Britain and entitlement continued by regulations` IS FALSE
        `income of the claimant` IS `a pension income of` 200
        `qualifying income of the claimant` IS 100
        `income of the other member` IS `no income`
        `qualifying income of the other member` IS 0
        `prescribed circumstances in which the income of the other member is not aggregated` IS FALSE
        `severely disabled` IS FALSE
        `claimant entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS FALSE
        `other member entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS FALSE
        `other member entitled to state pension credit` IS FALSE
        `regulations under section 3ZA(1) prescribe the claimant's case` IS FALSE
        `regulations under section 3(8) take the maximum savings credit to be nil` IS FALSE
        `excluded by section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 as amended by section 4(2)` IS FALSE
        `prescribed circumstances in which an amount below the prescribed amount is payable` IS FALSE
