§ `Dates and ages the text states (spc-dates)`

-- The date of Royal Assent is NOT in the deposited text (it has no square-bracketed date),
-- so the encoding defines it as NOTHING and the test asserts exactly that.
#ASSERT `the date of Royal Assent, as the deposited text states it` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Section 22(2): this section and sections 19 and 20 come into force on the passing. The
-- rule returns the day it is given; the day used here is INVENTED (1 January 2030).
#ASSERT `s 22(2) -- this section and sections 19 and 20 come into force on` (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2030 1 1

-- Section 22(3): the rest comes into force on the day appointed by order, which is an
-- input (invented here: 1 July 2030).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 22(3) -- a provision brought into force by order is in force on` (YearMonthDay 2030 6 30) `if the day appointed for it is` (YearMonthDay 2030 7 1))
#ASSERT `s 22(3) -- a provision brought into force by order is in force on` (YearMonthDay 2030 7 1) `if the day appointed for it is` (YearMonthDay 2030 7 1)
#ASSERT `s 22(3) -- a provision brought into force by order is in force on` (YearMonthDay 2030 7 2) `if the day appointed for it is` (YearMonthDay 2030 7 1)

-- Section 22(6): England and Wales and Scotland only.
#ASSERT `s 22(6) -- the extent of the Act` EQUALS "England and Wales and Scotland only"

-- The dates and ages the Act states.
#ASSERT `6 April 2016` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2016 4 6
#ASSERT `6 April 2009` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2009 4 6
#ASSERT `6 April 2014` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2014 4 6
#ASSERT `the age of 65` EQUALS 65
#ASSERT `the age of 75` EQUALS 75
#ASSERT `the age of 80` EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `the 5 years of an assessed income period` EQUALS 5

-- Section 17(3), the convention for attaining an age (fork F-04): the anniversary.
#ASSERT `the day on which the age is attained` (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) 65 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2015 5 10
#ASSERT `the age has been attained on` (YearMonthDay 2015 5 10) `by a person born on` (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) `at the age of` 65
#ASSERT NOT (`the age has been attained on` (YearMonthDay 2015 5 9) `by a person born on` (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) `at the age of` 65)
-- A person born on 29 February 2000 reaches 64 in a leap year (29 February 2064) and 65 in a
-- year with no 29 February; the lenient date constructor carries the day to 1 March 2065.
#ASSERT `the day on which the age is attained` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 29) 64 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2064 2 29
#ASSERT `the day on which the age is attained` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 29) 65 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2065 3 1
#ASSERT NOT (`the age has been attained on` (YearMonthDay 2065 2 28) `by a person born on` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 29) `at the age of` 65)
#ASSERT `the age has been attained on` (YearMonthDay 2065 3 1) `by a person born on` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 29) `at the age of` 65

§ `Interpretation (sections 15, 16 and 17)`

§§ `15 Income and capital`

-- Section 15(1): ten descriptions, in the Act's order, summed.
GIVETH AN Income
`income one to ten` MEANS
    Income WITH
        earnings IS 1
        `working tax credit` IS 2
        `retirement pension income` IS 3
        `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income` IS 4
        `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` IS 5
        `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description` IS 6
        `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS 7
        `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension` IS 8
        `income from capital` IS 9
        `income of a prescribed description` IS 10

#ASSERT `s 15(1) -- income` `income one to ten` EQUALS 55
#ASSERT `s 15(1) -- income` `no income` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 15(1) -- income` (`a pension income of` 150) EQUALS 150

-- Section 15(2): regulations MAY deem capital to yield income at a prescribed rate.
#ASSERT `s 15(2) -- income deemed to be yielded by capital` 1000 TRUE 0.05 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 15(2) -- income deemed to be yielded by capital` 1000 FALSE 0.05 EQUALS 0

§§ `16 Retirement pension income`

-- Section 16(1): every listed description is retirement pension income; the others
-- (earnings, working tax credit and so on) are not; and a payment by a former employer on
-- early retirement (paragraph (l)) is not if it was ordered by a court or made in
-- settlement of a claim.
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or its Northern Ireland counterpart` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `a Category A or Category B retirement pension` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `a shared additional pension` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `graduated retirement benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `a Category C or Category D retirement pension` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `age addition` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `income from an occupational pension scheme or a personal pension scheme` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `income from an overseas arrangement` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `income from a retirement annuity contract` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `income from annuities or insurance policies purchased or transferred to give effect to rights under a personal pension scheme or an overseas arrangement` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `income from annuities purchased or entered into to discharge liability for pension credits on divorce` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `a pension under section 5 of the Civil List Act 1837 or section 7 of the Civil List Act 1952` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `a payment by a former employer on account of early retirement on grounds of ill-health or disability` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `a payment by a former employer on account of early retirement on grounds of ill-health or disability` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `a payment at regular intervals under an equity release scheme` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `a payment under the Financial Assistance Scheme Regulations 2005` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` earnings FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `working tax credit` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `income from capital` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `PPF periodic payments` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` `income from an annuity contract other than retirement pension income` FALSE)

§§ `17 Other interpretation provisions`

-- "Couple": limb (a) married or civil partners AND the same household; limb (b) NOT married
-- or civil partners, living together as a married couple or civil partners, otherwise
-- than in prescribed circumstances.
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- couple` `a married couple in one household`
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- couple` `an unmarried couple living together`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- couple` `a single person`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- couple` `an unmarried couple living together in prescribed circumstances`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- couple` `a married pair in different households`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- couple` `a married pair in different households who live together`)

-- "Foreign social security benefit": paid under the law of a country outside the UK AND in the
-- nature of social security.
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- foreign social security benefit` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- foreign social security benefit` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- foreign social security benefit` FALSE TRUE)

-- "Foreign war disablement pension": granted by a foreign government AND (a) or (b).
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- foreign war disablement pension` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- foreign war disablement pension` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- foreign war disablement pension` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- foreign war disablement pension` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- "Foreign war widow's or widower's pension": the same shape.
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- foreign war widow's or widower's pension` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- foreign war widow's or widower's pension` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- foreign war widow's or widower's pension` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- foreign war widow's or widower's pension` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- "War disablement pension" and "war widow's or widower's pension": (a) or (b).
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- war disablement pension` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- war disablement pension` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- war disablement pension` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- war widow's or widower's pension` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- war widow's or widower's pension` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- war widow's or widower's pension` FALSE FALSE)

-- "Working tax credit": a working tax credit under the Tax Credits Act 2002 to which the person is entitled.
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- working tax credit` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- working tax credit` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- working tax credit` FALSE TRUE)

-- "PPF periodic payments": (a) or (b).
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- PPF periodic payments` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- PPF periodic payments` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- PPF periodic payments` FALSE FALSE)

§ `Small rules in sections 1 and 3 (unit tests)`

-- Section 1(6): the qualifying age.
#ASSERT `s 1(6) -- the day the person attains the qualifying age` `woman W1` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2010 5 10
#ASSERT `s 1(6) -- the day the person attains the qualifying age` `man M1` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2010 5 10
#ASSERT `s 1(6) -- the day the person attains the qualifying age` `woman W3` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 1 1
#ASSERT `s 1(6) -- has attained the qualifying age on` (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) `woman W1`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1(6) -- has attained the qualifying age on` (YearMonthDay 2010 5 9) `woman W1`)
#ASSERT `s 1(6) -- has attained the qualifying age on` (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) `man M1`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1(6) -- has attained the qualifying age on` (YearMonthDay 2010 5 9) `man M1`)

-- Section 3(1)(a): pensionable age attained BEFORE 6 April 2016 and 65 attained by the day.
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(a) -- has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65` `test day` `woman W1`
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(a) -- has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65` `test day` `woman E1`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(a) -- has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65` `test day` `woman E2`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(a) -- has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65` `test day` `woman W3`)
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(a) -- has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65` (YearMonthDay 2015 5 10) `woman W1`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(a) -- has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65` (YearMonthDay 2015 5 9) `woman W1`)
-- For a man, section 3(1)(a) reads his OWN pensionable age (2015), not his qualifying age (2010).
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(a) -- has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65` `test day` `man M1`

§ `The small rules of sections 1 to 4 (unit tests)`

-- Each helper is asserted directly, from the case it is called on (the working for each case is in its
-- comment above). The cases are the ones the rest of this file already uses.

§§ `Section 1(2): the three conditions`
-- A0 is in Great Britain; M1 is not and is not within the temporary-absence rule; M2 is away but the regulations continue entitlement.
#ASSERT `s 1(2)(a) -- he is in Great Britain` `case A0`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1(2)(a) -- he is in Great Britain` `case M1`)
#ASSERT `s 1(2)(a) -- he is in Great Britain` `case M2`
-- K2a is W1 on 9 May 2010 (a day short of the qualifying age); K2b is her on 10 May 2010.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1(2)(b) -- he has attained the qualifying age` `case K2a`)
#ASSERT `s 1(2)(b) -- he has attained the qualifying age` `case K2b`
-- A0 has no income: the guarantee credit condition is met (2(1)(a)). C2 has income one above the guarantee and too little qualifying income for the savings credit: neither.
#ASSERT `s 1(2)(c) -- he satisfies the guarantee credit condition or the savings credit conditions` `case A0` `P0`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1(2)(c) -- he satisfies the guarantee credit condition or the savings credit conditions` `case C2` `P0`)
#ASSERT `s 1(2) -- the conditions of section 1(2) are met` `case A0` `P0`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1(2) -- the conditions of section 1(2) are met` `case M1` `P0`)

§§ `Section 1(3)(b): entitled to a savings credit`
-- A0 has no income and no qualifying income: no savings credit. D1 (income 210) has one, 25.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1(3)(b) -- entitled to a savings credit` `case A0` `P0`)
#ASSERT `s 1(3)(b) -- entitled to a savings credit` `case D1` `P0`

§§ `Section 1(4): entitled under sections 1 to 5; displacement; section 17(1)`
#ASSERT `s 1(4) -- entitled to state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` `case A0` `P0`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1(4) -- entitled to state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` `case C2` `P0`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1(4) -- entitled to state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` `case I1` `P0`)
#ASSERT `s 1(4) -- regulations or a pilot scheme may displace the Act's rules for the case` `case P1`
#ASSERT `s 1(4) -- regulations or a pilot scheme may displace the Act's rules for the case` `case P3`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1(4) -- regulations or a pilot scheme may displace the Act's rules for the case` `case P2`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1(4) -- regulations or a pilot scheme may displace the Act's rules for the case` `case A0`)
-- A0 has claimed and nothing restricts it; N1 has not claimed; N2 is restricted under section 27.
#ASSERT `s 17(1) -- entitled to state pension credit` `case A0` `P0`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- entitled to state pension credit` `case N1` `P0`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) -- entitled to state pension credit` `case N2` `P0`)

§§ `Section 2: the minimum guarantee and its parts`
-- A0 is single: the standard minimum guarantee is the lower single figure, 200. E1 is a couple: 300.
#ASSERT `s 2(5) -- the standard minimum guarantee` `case A0` `P0` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 2(5) -- the standard minimum guarantee` `case E1` `P0` EQUALS 300
-- The substitution of section 2(6) replaces it in 2(3)(a) only: G1 with 250 substituted gives 250; A0 gives 200.
#ASSERT `s 2(3)(a) -- the amount that stands for the standard minimum guarantee in the appropriate minimum guarantee` `case G1` `P0 with 250 substituted for the standard minimum guarantee` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `s 2(3)(a) -- the amount that stands for the standard minimum guarantee in the appropriate minimum guarantee` `case A0` `P0` EQUALS 200
-- The additions: F1 single, severely disabled (+50) and with an allowance (+40): 90. F2 couple, BOTH members have the allowance: one amount, 40.
-- F3 only the other member has it: 40. F4 single, other member's allowance ignored: 0. F5 couple, claimant severely disabled only: 50. A0: 0.
#ASSERT `s 2(3)(b) -- the prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` `case F1` `P0` EQUALS 90

#ASSERT `s 2(3)(b) -- the prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` `case F2` `P0` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `s 2(3)(b) -- the prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` `case F3` `P0` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `s 2(3)(b) -- the prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` `case F4` `P0` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2(3)(b) -- the prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` `case F5` `P0` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 2(3)(b) -- the prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` `case A0` `P0` EQUALS 0
-- Whether an allowance amount is included (section 2(8)): F1, F2, F3 yes; F4 (single: (b) needs a couple), F5 (severe disability only) and A0 no.
#ASSERT `s 2(8) -- an amount is included for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` `case F1`
#ASSERT `s 2(8) -- an amount is included for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` `case F2`
#ASSERT `s 2(8) -- an amount is included for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` `case F3`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(8) -- an amount is included for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` `case F4`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(8) -- an amount is included for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` `case F5`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(8) -- an amount is included for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` `case A0`)

§§ `Section 3(5): the figure that stands for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B`
-- G2: 250 substituted AND a higher amount 270 prescribed: 270. G3: a higher amount 270 prescribed but NO substitution in play: the appropriate minimum guarantee itself, 200 (single, no additions).
-- G1: substitution 250 but no higher amount prescribed: the appropriate minimum guarantee, 250. A0: 200.
#ASSERT `s 3(5) -- the figure that stands for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` `case G2` `P0 with 250 substituted and 270 as the higher amount in amount B` EQUALS 270
#ASSERT `s 3(5) -- the figure that stands for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` `case G3` `P0 with only a higher amount of 270 and no substitution` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 3(5) -- the figure that stands for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` `case G1` `P0 with 250 substituted for the standard minimum guarantee` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `s 3(5) -- the figure that stands for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` `case A0` `P0` EQUALS 200

§§ `Section 4(2): section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999`
-- I4 is excluded; A0 is not.
#ASSERT `s 4(2) -- excluded under section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999` `case I4`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4(2) -- excluded under section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999` `case A0`)

§ `Sections 11 to 14 and 18 to 21 (spc-part-misc, spc-part-final)`

-- Section 12(1): all three conditions, or the section does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 12(1) -- section 12 applies to the case` `case P1`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(1) -- section 12 applies to the case` `case P2`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(1) -- section 12 applies to the case` `case A0`)

-- Section 18A(5): a pilot scheme may displace provisions of the Act for the case.
#ASSERT `s 18A(5) -- a pilot scheme may displace provisions of the Act for the case` `case P3`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18A(5) -- a pilot scheme may displace provisions of the Act for the case` `case A0`)

-- Section 18A(1): a pilot scheme period must not exceed 12 months.
#ASSERT `s 18A(1) -- the period of the pilot scheme does not exceed 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2030 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2031 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18A(1) -- the period of the pilot scheme does not exceed 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2030 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2031 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18A(1) -- the period of the pilot scheme does not exceed 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2030 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2030 2 28))
-- A scheme starting on 29 February 2032 (a leap year): the next year has no 29 February, so
-- the same calendar day is 1 March 2033 and the last permitted day is 28 February 2033.
#ASSERT `s 18A(1) -- the period of the pilot scheme does not exceed 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2032 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2033 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18A(1) -- the period of the pilot scheme does not exceed 12 months` (YearMonthDay 2032 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2033 3 1))

§ `Retirement provision (sections 6 to 10)`

