§§ `6 Duty to specify assessed income period for pre-6 April 2016 awards`

-- Section 6(3)(c): on or after the claimant's 65th birthday, or the other member's of a couple.
#ASSERT `s 6(3)(c) -- the decision takes effect on or after the day the claimant, or the other member of a couple if earlier, attains the age of 65` `case R1` (YearMonthDay 2015 5 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6(3)(c) -- the decision takes effect on or after the day the claimant, or the other member of a couple if earlier, attains the age of 65` `case R1` (YearMonthDay 2015 5 9))
-- A couple: the claimant W3 is far from 65 but the other member W1 reached 65 on 10 May 2015.
#ASSERT `s 6(3)(c) -- the decision takes effect on or after the day the claimant, or the other member of a couple if earlier, attains the age of 65` `case R2` (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6(3)(c) -- the decision takes effect on or after the day the claimant, or the other member of a couple if earlier, attains the age of 65` `case R2` (YearMonthDay 2015 5 9))
-- The same claimant living alone: the other member does not count.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6(3)(c) -- the decision takes effect on or after the day the claimant, or the other member of a couple if earlier, attains the age of 65` `case R3` (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1))

-- Sections 6(3) and 6(4): the two cases.
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- the first case` `case R1` `decision D-A`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6(3) -- the first case` `case R1` `decision D-before65`)
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- the first case` `case R1` `decision D-on65`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6(3) -- the first case` `case R1` `decision D-refusal`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6(3) -- the first case` `case R1` `decision D-appeal`)
#ASSERT `s 6(4) -- the second case` `case R1` `decision D-appeal`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6(4) -- the second case` `case R1` `decision D-A`)

-- Section 6(2): prevented by an earlier period or by prescribed circumstances.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- the Secretary of State is prevented from specifying a period` `decision D-previous`
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- the Secretary of State is prevented from specifying a period` `decision D-other`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6(2) -- the Secretary of State is prevented from specifying a period` `decision D-A`)

-- Section 6(1): what the section requires (the Secretary of State's view under section 9(2) is an input).
#ASSERT `s 6(1) -- what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State on the decision` `case R1` `decision D-A` FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State must specify an assessed income period`
#ASSERT `s 6(1) -- what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State on the decision` `case R1` `decision D-A` TRUE EQUALS `The Secretary of State need not specify an assessed income period, and any period specified must be shorter than 5 years`
#ASSERT `s 6(1) -- what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State on the decision` `case R1` `decision D-previous` FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State is prevented from specifying an assessed income period`
#ASSERT `s 6(1) -- what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State on the decision` `case R1` `decision D-previous` TRUE EQUALS `The Secretary of State is prevented from specifying an assessed income period`
#ASSERT `s 6(1) -- what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State on the decision` `case R1` `decision D-other` FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State is prevented from specifying an assessed income period`
#ASSERT `s 6(1) -- what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State on the decision` `case R1` `decision D-apr5` FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State must specify an assessed income period`
#ASSERT `s 6(1) -- what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State on the decision` `case R1` `decision D-apr6` FALSE EQUALS `Section 6 does not apply to the decision`
#ASSERT `s 6(1) -- what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State on the decision` `case R1` `decision D-before65` FALSE EQUALS `Section 6 does not apply to the decision`
#ASSERT `s 6(1) -- what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State on the decision` `case R1` `decision D-on65` FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State must specify an assessed income period`
#ASSERT `s 6(1) -- what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State on the decision` `case R1` `decision D-refusal` FALSE EQUALS `Section 6 does not apply to the decision`
#ASSERT `s 6(1) -- what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State on the decision` `case R1` `decision D-appeal` FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State must specify an assessed income period`

§§ `7 Fixing of claimant's retirement provision for assessed income period`

-- Section 7(6)(a): the Great Britain state benefits are excluded; their Northern Ireland
-- counterparts are not, on a literal reading (fork F-12).
#ASSERT `s 7(6)(a) -- a benefit under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or the Contributions and Benefits Act` `a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or its Northern Ireland counterpart` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(6)(a) -- a benefit under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or the Contributions and Benefits Act` `a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or its Northern Ireland counterpart` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 7(6)(a) -- a benefit under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or the Contributions and Benefits Act` `a Category A or Category B retirement pension` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(6)(a) -- a benefit under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or the Contributions and Benefits Act` `age addition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(6)(a) -- a benefit under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or the Contributions and Benefits Act` `income from an occupational pension scheme or a personal pension scheme` FALSE)

-- Section 7(6): retirement provision.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or its Northern Ireland counterpart` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or its Northern Ireland counterpart` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `a Category A or Category B retirement pension` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `a Category A or Category B retirement pension` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `income from an occupational pension scheme or a personal pension scheme` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `income from a retirement annuity contract` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `a payment by a former employer on account of early retirement on grounds of ill-health or disability` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `a payment by a former employer on account of early retirement on grounds of ill-health or disability` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `income from an annuity contract other than retirement pension income` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `income from capital` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `PPF periodic payments` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(6) -- retirement provision` earnings FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `working tax credit` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(6) -- retirement provision` `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` FALSE FALSE)

-- E-pension: assessed amount 100, not income from capital, included in the determination; prescribed variations +10 from 1 April 2021, +5 from 1 April 2022, -7 from 1 June 2022. Only increases count for an element that is not income from capital (section 7(4)(a)).
GIVETH AN `Element of retirement provision`
`element E-pension` MEANS
    `Element of retirement provision` WITH
        `assessed amount` IS 100
        `income from capital` IS FALSE
        `included in the claimant's income as determined for the relevant decision` IS TRUE
        `variations prescribed under section 7(4)` IS LIST (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2021 4 1, `amount of the variation` IS 10), (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2022 4 1, `amount of the variation` IS 5), (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2022 6 1, `amount of the variation` IS -7)
        `prescribed circumstances in which the assessed amount is not deemed to vary` IS FALSE

-- E-capital: the same variations, but the element IS income from capital, so a decrease counts too (section 7(4)(b)).
GIVETH AN `Element of retirement provision`
`element E-capital` MEANS
    `Element of retirement provision` WITH
        `assessed amount` IS 100
        `income from capital` IS TRUE
        `included in the claimant's income as determined for the relevant decision` IS TRUE
        `variations prescribed under section 7(4)` IS LIST (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2021 4 1, `amount of the variation` IS 10), (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2022 4 1, `amount of the variation` IS 5), (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2022 6 1, `amount of the variation` IS -7)
        `prescribed circumstances in which the assessed amount is not deemed to vary` IS FALSE

-- E-absent: the relevant decision found the claimant's income did NOT include this element (section 7(5)): taken not to include it throughout.
GIVETH AN `Element of retirement provision`
`element E-absent` MEANS
    `Element of retirement provision` WITH
        `assessed amount` IS 100
        `income from capital` IS FALSE
        `included in the claimant's income as determined for the relevant decision` IS FALSE
        `variations prescribed under section 7(4)` IS LIST (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2021 4 1, `amount of the variation` IS 10), (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2022 4 1, `amount of the variation` IS 5), (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2022 6 1, `amount of the variation` IS -7)
        `prescribed circumstances in which the assessed amount is not deemed to vary` IS FALSE

-- E-excepted: prescribed circumstances in which the assessed amount is not deemed to vary.
GIVETH AN `Element of retirement provision`
`element E-excepted` MEANS
    `Element of retirement provision` WITH
        `assessed amount` IS 100
        `income from capital` IS FALSE
        `included in the claimant's income as determined for the relevant decision` IS TRUE
        `variations prescribed under section 7(4)` IS LIST (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2021 4 1, `amount of the variation` IS 10), (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2022 4 1, `amount of the variation` IS 5), (Variation WITH `day the variation takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2022 6 1, `amount of the variation` IS -7)
        `prescribed circumstances in which the assessed amount is not deemed to vary` IS TRUE

-- Section 7(3) to (5): the amount of the element on a day of the period.
#ASSERT `s 7(3) to (5) -- the amount of the element on` (YearMonthDay 2021 3 31) `element E-pension` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 7(3) to (5) -- the amount of the element on` (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1) `element E-pension` EQUALS 110
#ASSERT `s 7(3) to (5) -- the amount of the element on` (YearMonthDay 2022 3 31) `element E-pension` EQUALS 110
#ASSERT `s 7(3) to (5) -- the amount of the element on` (YearMonthDay 2022 4 1) `element E-pension` EQUALS 115
#ASSERT `s 7(3) to (5) -- the amount of the element on` (YearMonthDay 2022 12 31) `element E-pension` EQUALS 115
#ASSERT `s 7(3) to (5) -- the amount of the element on` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 31) `element E-capital` EQUALS 115
#ASSERT `s 7(3) to (5) -- the amount of the element on` (YearMonthDay 2022 6 1) `element E-capital` EQUALS 108
#ASSERT `s 7(3) to (5) -- the amount of the element on` (YearMonthDay 2022 12 31) `element E-absent` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 7(3) to (5) -- the amount of the element on` (YearMonthDay 2022 12 31) `element E-excepted` EQUALS 100

§§ `8 Fresh determinations increasing claimant's entitlement`

-- Section 8(1)/(2): (a) a section 10 decision; the amount before 100 and under the new decision
-- (and what it would be apart from the fresh determinations); (c) the increase is the result
-- of the fresh determinations. Arguments: (a), (c), before, after, apart.
#ASSERT `s 8(1), (2) -- fresh determinations may be made` TRUE TRUE 100 120 110
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(1), (2) -- fresh determinations may be made` FALSE TRUE 100 120 110)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(1), (2) -- fresh determinations may be made` TRUE FALSE 100 120 100)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(1), (2) -- fresh determinations may be made` TRUE TRUE 100 100 90)
-- A reduction counts if smaller than it would have been apart from the fresh determinations:
-- 100 to 90 (a reduction of 10) where it would have been 100 to 80 (20).
#ASSERT `s 8(1), (2) -- fresh determinations may be made` TRUE FALSE 100 90 80
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(1), (2) -- fresh determinations may be made` TRUE FALSE 100 90 90)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(1), (2) -- fresh determinations may be made` TRUE FALSE 100 90 95)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(1), (2) -- fresh determinations may be made` FALSE FALSE 100 90 80)

-- Section 8(3): from the day the new decision takes effect (inclusive), the fresh determination governs.
#ASSERT `s 8(3) -- which determination governs on` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 14) `when the new decision takes effect on` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 15) EQUALS `The determination it replaces governs`
#ASSERT `s 8(3) -- which determination governs on` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 15) `when the new decision takes effect on` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 15) EQUALS `The fresh determination governs`
#ASSERT `s 8(3) -- which determination governs on` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 16) `when the new decision takes effect on` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 15) EQUALS `The fresh determination governs`

§§ `9 Duration of assessed income period`

-- Section 9(1): under 75 on the day the decision takes effect, five years; 75 or over, indefinite.
-- A claimant born 1 March 1940 is 75 on 1 March 2015.
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the length of the assessed income period for a decision taking effect on` (YearMonthDay 2015 2 28) `for a claimant born on` (YearMonthDay 1940 3 1) EQUALS `Five years beginning with the day the relevant decision takes effect`
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the length of the assessed income period for a decision taking effect on` (YearMonthDay 2015 3 1) `for a claimant born on` (YearMonthDay 1940 3 1) EQUALS `An indefinite period beginning with that day`
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the length of the assessed income period for a decision taking effect on` (YearMonthDay 2015 3 2) `for a claimant born on` (YearMonthDay 1940 3 1) EQUALS `An indefinite period beginning with that day`

-- Section 9(1)(a): the first day after five years beginning with a day.
#ASSERT `s 9(1)(a) -- the first day after a period of 5 years beginning with` (YearMonthDay 2014 4 10) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 4 10
#ASSERT `s 9(1)(a) -- the first day after a period of 5 years beginning with` (YearMonthDay 2012 2 29) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2017 3 1

-- Section 9(2)(b): where the Secretary of State considers the particulars not typical, a period
-- he does specify begins with the decision day and is shorter than 5 years. Arguments:
-- decision day, first day, last day of the period specified, and his consideration.
-- Five years from 1 June 2015 would end on 31 May 2020.
#ASSERT `s 9(2)(b) -- the period specified complies` (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 6 1) TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(2)(b) -- the period specified complies` (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 5 30) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(2)(b) -- the period specified complies` (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 5 31) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(2)(b) -- the period specified complies` (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 2) (YearMonthDay 2018 6 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 9(2)(b) -- the period specified complies` (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 5 31) FALSE

-- Section 9(6): brought to an end, on or after 6 April 2009 but before 6 April 2014, by expiry of
-- a period of 5 years or more, and the claimant is aged 80 or over then. Arguments: the last day of
-- the period, and the date of birth. A claimant born 6 April 1929 is 80 on 6 April 2009.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(6) -- an assessed income period brought to an end on` (YearMonthDay 2009 4 5) `by expiry, for a claimant born on` (YearMonthDay 1925 1 1) `is treated as continuing indefinitely`)
#ASSERT `s 9(6) -- an assessed income period brought to an end on` (YearMonthDay 2009 4 6) `by expiry, for a claimant born on` (YearMonthDay 1925 1 1) `is treated as continuing indefinitely`
#ASSERT `s 9(6) -- an assessed income period brought to an end on` (YearMonthDay 2014 4 5) `by expiry, for a claimant born on` (YearMonthDay 1925 1 1) `is treated as continuing indefinitely`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(6) -- an assessed income period brought to an end on` (YearMonthDay 2014 4 6) `by expiry, for a claimant born on` (YearMonthDay 1925 1 1) `is treated as continuing indefinitely`)
#ASSERT `s 9(6) -- an assessed income period brought to an end on` (YearMonthDay 2009 4 6) `by expiry, for a claimant born on` (YearMonthDay 1929 4 6) `is treated as continuing indefinitely`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(6) -- an assessed income period brought to an end on` (YearMonthDay 2009 4 6) `by expiry, for a claimant born on` (YearMonthDay 1929 4 7) `is treated as continuing indefinitely`)

-- P-plain: begins 1 June 2015, no couple change, no further prescribed time.
GIVETH AN `Assessed income period`
`period P-plain` MEANS
    `Assessed income period` WITH
        `day the relevant decision takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2015 6 1
        `first day after that day on which the claimant becomes or ceases to be a member of a couple` IS NOTHING
        `first further time prescribed under section 9(5)` IS NOTHING
        `prescribed circumstances in which the period does not end under section 9(4)` IS FALSE

-- P-couple: begins 1 June 2015; the claimant becomes a member of a couple on 1 January 2017.
GIVETH AN `Assessed income period`
`period P-couple` MEANS
    `Assessed income period` WITH
        `day the relevant decision takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2015 6 1
        `first day after that day on which the claimant becomes or ceases to be a member of a couple` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2017 1 1)
        `first further time prescribed under section 9(5)` IS NOTHING
        `prescribed circumstances in which the period does not end under section 9(4)` IS FALSE

-- P-regs: begins 1 June 2015; regulations under section 9(5) prescribe 9 September 2016 as a further time.
GIVETH AN `Assessed income period`
`period P-regs` MEANS
    `Assessed income period` WITH
        `day the relevant decision takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2015 6 1
        `first day after that day on which the claimant becomes or ceases to be a member of a couple` IS NOTHING
        `first further time prescribed under section 9(5)` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 9 9)
        `prescribed circumstances in which the period does not end under section 9(4)` IS FALSE

-- P-circ: as P-couple, but prescribed circumstances mean section 9(4) does not end the period; and a section 9(5) time of 9 September 2016.
GIVETH AN `Assessed income period`
`period P-circ` MEANS
    `Assessed income period` WITH
        `day the relevant decision takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2015 6 1
        `first day after that day on which the claimant becomes or ceases to be a member of a couple` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2017 1 1)
        `first further time prescribed under section 9(5)` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 9 9)
        `prescribed circumstances in which the period does not end under section 9(4)` IS TRUE

-- P-circ-only: as P-couple but prescribed circumstances apply, and no section 9(5) time.
GIVETH AN `Assessed income period`
`period P-circ-only` MEANS
    `Assessed income period` WITH
        `day the relevant decision takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2015 6 1
        `first day after that day on which the claimant becomes or ceases to be a member of a couple` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2017 1 1)
        `first further time prescribed under section 9(5)` IS NOTHING
        `prescribed circumstances in which the period does not end under section 9(4)` IS TRUE

-- P-on65: begins 10 May 2015, W1's own 65th birthday.
GIVETH AN `Assessed income period`
`period P-on65` MEANS
    `Assessed income period` WITH
        `day the relevant decision takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2015 5 10
        `first day after that day on which the claimant becomes or ceases to be a member of a couple` IS NOTHING
        `first further time prescribed under section 9(5)` IS NOTHING
        `prescribed circumstances in which the period does not end under section 9(4)` IS FALSE

-- P-2008: begins 7 April 2008.
GIVETH AN `Assessed income period`
`period P-2008` MEANS
    `Assessed income period` WITH
        `day the relevant decision takes effect` IS YearMonthDay 2008 4 7
        `first day after that day on which the claimant becomes or ceases to be a member of a couple` IS NOTHING
        `first further time prescribed under section 9(5)` IS NOTHING
        `prescribed circumstances in which the period does not end under section 9(4)` IS FALSE

-- Section 9(4), (5) and 9 as a whole: the first day on which the period is no longer in force.
-- W1 is 65 on 10 May 2015 and 75 on 10 May 2025; on 1 June 2015 she is under 75 so the period is 5 years.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force` `case R1` `period P-plain` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1)
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the assessed income period is in force on` (YearMonthDay 2020 5 31) `case R1` `period P-plain`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9 -- the assessed income period is in force on` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) `case R1` `period P-plain`)
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the assessed income period is in force on` (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) `case R1` `period P-plain`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9 -- the assessed income period is in force on` (YearMonthDay 2015 5 31) `case R1` `period P-plain`)
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force` `case R1` `period P-couple` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2017 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force` `case R1` `period P-regs` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 9 9)
-- Prescribed circumstances: the 9(4) event is disregarded, the section 9(5) time and the five years are not.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force` `case R1` `period P-circ` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 9 9)
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force` `case R1` `period P-circ-only` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1)
-- W1's own 65th birthday (10 May 2015) is not a time during a period that begins on or after it:
-- a period beginning ON that day is not ended by it (fork F-13).
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force` `case R1` `period P-on65` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 5 10)
-- A couple, claimant W1 and other member W2, whose 65th birthday is 3 March 2017: it ends the period (9(4)(d)).
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force` `case R4` `period P-plain` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2017 3 3)
-- W5 was 75 on 1 January 2013: an indefinite period, no ending day known; still in force today.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force` `case R5` `period P-plain` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the assessed income period is in force on` `test day` `case R5` `period P-plain`
-- A claimant under 75 at the start cannot be 80 at the end of five years: section 9(6) never carries
-- on a period that section 9(1)(a) fixed (finding 9). W6, born 7 April 1934, is 74 on 7 April 2008:
-- five years to 7 April 2013, inside the 9(6) window, yet aged 78 then, so it ends.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force` `case R6` `period P-2008` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 4 7)

§§ `10 Effect of variations under section 7(4)`

-- Section 10 applies where a period is in force AND an element is varied under section 7(4)
-- AND the variation affects the computation. Then, from the commencing date, the changed
-- amount is payable. Before the commencing date section 10 is silent; the existing award's
-- amount (50 here, invented) is returned (fork F-23). Where section 10 does not apply the
-- rule answers NOTHING: the section says nothing about what is payable.
#ASSERT `s 10(2), (3) -- the amount of state pension credit payable on` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 31) `given the commencing date` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `with an assessed income period in force` TRUE `and a variation of an element` TRUE `that affects the computation` TRUE `from the amount before` 50 `to the amount after` 60 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 10(2), (3) -- the amount of state pension credit payable on` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `given the commencing date` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `with an assessed income period in force` TRUE `and a variation of an element` TRUE `that affects the computation` TRUE `from the amount before` 50 `to the amount after` 60 EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT `s 10(2), (3) -- the amount of state pension credit payable on` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 2) `given the commencing date` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `with an assessed income period in force` TRUE `and a variation of an element` TRUE `that affects the computation` TRUE `from the amount before` 50 `to the amount after` 60 EQUALS JUST 60
-- A reduction works the same way (section 10(2): 'increased or reduced').
#ASSERT `s 10(2), (3) -- the amount of state pension credit payable on` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `given the commencing date` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `with an assessed income period in force` TRUE `and a variation of an element` TRUE `that affects the computation` TRUE `from the amount before` 50 `to the amount after` 40 EQUALS JUST 40
-- Not within section 10: no period in force, or no variation, or it does not affect the computation.
#ASSERT `s 10(2), (3) -- the amount of state pension credit payable on` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 2) `given the commencing date` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `with an assessed income period in force` FALSE `and a variation of an element` TRUE `that affects the computation` TRUE `from the amount before` 50 `to the amount after` 60 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(2), (3) -- the amount of state pension credit payable on` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 2) `given the commencing date` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `with an assessed income period in force` TRUE `and a variation of an element` FALSE `that affects the computation` TRUE `from the amount before` 50 `to the amount after` 60 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(2), (3) -- the amount of state pension credit payable on` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 2) `given the commencing date` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `with an assessed income period in force` TRUE `and a variation of an element` TRUE `that affects the computation` FALSE `from the amount before` 50 `to the amount after` 60 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 10(3): the same amount continues.
#ASSERT `s 10(2), (3) -- the amount of state pension credit payable on` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 2) `given the commencing date` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `with an assessed income period in force` TRUE `and a variation of an element` TRUE `that affects the computation` TRUE `from the amount before` 50 `to the amount after` 50 EQUALS JUST 50

-- Section 10(2): no further decision of the Secretary of State is needed when section 10 applies;
-- when it does not apply the Act is silent.
#ASSERT `s 10(2) -- whether a further decision of the Secretary of State is needed for the changed amount to be payable` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `The Act says no`
#ASSERT `s 10(2) -- whether a further decision of the Secretary of State is needed for the changed amount to be payable` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not covered by this encoding`
#ASSERT `s 10(2) -- whether a further decision of the Secretary of State is needed for the changed amount to be payable` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not covered by this encoding`
#ASSERT `s 10(2) -- whether a further decision of the Secretary of State is needed for the changed amount to be payable` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not covered by this encoding`

§ `The small rules of sections 6 to 9 (unit tests)`

-- The earlier of two optional days (an encoding helper, not a provision): the earlier of two, whichever one there is, or none.
#ASSERT `encoding helper -- the earlier of two optional days` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `encoding helper -- the earlier of two optional days` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT `encoding helper -- the earlier of two optional days` NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1)
#ASSERT `encoding helper -- the earlier of two optional days` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT `encoding helper -- the earlier of two optional days` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT `encoding helper -- the earlier of two optional days` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1)

-- Section 9(4), (5): the first day on which a period is no longer in force because an event ends it.
-- R1 (single, 65 before the period starts): no event, so none. P-couple: a couple event on 1 January 2017. P-regs: a prescribed time 9 September 2016.
-- R4: the other member (W2) is 65 on 3 March 2017. P-circ-only: prescribed circumstances disapply 9(4), no 9(5) time, so none.

#ASSERT `s 9(4), (5) -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force because it ends` `case R1` `period P-plain` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(4), (5) -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force because it ends` `case R1` `period P-couple` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2017 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 9(4), (5) -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force because it ends` `case R1` `period P-regs` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 9 9)
#ASSERT `s 9(4), (5) -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force because it ends` `case R4` `period P-plain` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2017 3 3)
#ASSERT `s 9(4), (5) -- the first day on which the assessed income period is no longer in force because it ends` `case R1` `period P-circ-only` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Schedules 1 to 3 (spc-sch1, spc-sch2, spc-sch3)`

§§ `Schedule 1`

-- Paragraph 3(3A): evidence about the likelihood of future changes, needed to decide whether to
-- specify an assessed income period, or its length.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(3A) -- the information or evidence is within what the regulations may require for state pension credit` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(3A) -- the information or evidence is within what the regulations may require for state pension credit` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 1 para 3(3A) -- the information or evidence is within what the regulations may require for state pension credit` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 1 para 3(3A) -- the information or evidence is within what the regulations may require for state pension credit` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- Paragraph 12: the four decisions about an assessed income period against which an appeal lies.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 12 -- an appeal lies against` `A decision whether to specify a period as an assessed income period under section 6` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 12 -- an appeal lies against` `A decision as to the period to be so specified` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 12 -- an appeal lies against` `A decision whether an assessed income period comes to an end by virtue of section 9(4) or (5)` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 12 -- an appeal lies against` `A decision as to when the assessed income period so ends` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
-- A decision of any other kind is not answered by the paragraph.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 12 -- an appeal lies against` `A decision of another kind` EQUALS `Not covered by this encoding`

-- Paragraph 13: a period of less than a week; the prescribed amount (12 here, invented); 7 days is a week.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 13 -- the amount payable for a period of` 6 `days` `given the prescribed amount` 12 EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 13 -- the amount payable for a period of` 6 `days` `given the prescribed amount` 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 13 -- the amount payable for a period of` 7 `days` `given the prescribed amount` 12 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 13 -- the amount payable for a period of` 8 `days` `given the prescribed amount` 12 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Schedule 2`

-- S2a: W1 on 9 May 2010, before she attains the qualifying age; the other member (W2) IS entitled to state pension credit; a married couple in one household.
GIVETH A Case
`case S2a` MEANS
    Case WITH
        `day tested` IS YearMonthDay 2010 5 9
        claimant IS `woman W1`
        `other member of the couple` IS `woman W2`
        household IS `a married couple in one household`
        `in Great Britain` IS TRUE
        `temporarily absent from Great Britain and entitlement continued by regulations` IS FALSE
        `income of the claimant` IS `no income`
        `qualifying income of the claimant` IS 0
        `income of the other member` IS `no income`
        `qualifying income of the other member` IS 0
        `prescribed circumstances in which the income of the other member is not aggregated` IS FALSE
        `severely disabled` IS FALSE
        `claimant entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS FALSE
        `other member entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` IS FALSE
        `other member entitled to state pension credit` IS TRUE
        `regulations under section 3ZA(1) prescribe the claimant's case` IS FALSE
        `regulations under section 3(8) take the maximum savings credit to be nil` IS FALSE
        `excluded by section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 as amended by section 4(2)` IS FALSE
        `prescribed circumstances in which an amount below the prescribed amount is payable` IS FALSE
        `a claim has been made and the Administration Act section 1 conditions are met` IS TRUE
        `entitlement restricted by section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998` IS FALSE
        `husband or wife by a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy` IS FALSE
        `either party to the marriage has a spouse additional to the other party` IS FALSE
        `person, other party and additional spouse members of the same household` IS FALSE
        `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies` IS FALSE

-- Paragraph 2: the conditions inserted into section 124(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act.
-- Single, not yet at the qualifying age (case K2a): both inserted conditions are met.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2 -- the conditions inserted into section 124(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act are met` `case K2a` FALSE
-- At the qualifying age (case K2b): condition (aa) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 2 para 2 -- the conditions inserted into section 124(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act are met` `case K2b` FALSE)
-- A couple, the other member entitled to state pension credit: condition (g) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 2 para 2 -- the conditions inserted into section 124(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act are met` `case S2a` TRUE)
-- A couple, the other member NOT entitled: both met.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2 -- the conditions inserted into section 124(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act are met` `case K2a` TRUE

-- Paragraph 4: the qualifying age is section 1(6)'s.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4 -- the day the person attains the qualifying age for state pension credit` `woman W1` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2010 5 10
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4 -- the day the person attains the qualifying age for state pension credit` `man M1` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2010 5 10

-- Paragraph 17 (section 159B of the Administration Act), amounts 50 (before) and 60 (after).
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 17 -- the amount of state pension credit payable on` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 31) `under section 159B given the commencing date` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `with an award in force` TRUE `and an alteration in a component` TRUE `or in benefit income` FALSE `or in a jobseeker's allowance component` FALSE `or in a war pension` FALSE `that affects the computation` TRUE `outside any prescribed exception` FALSE `from the amount before` 50 `to the amount after` 60 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 17 -- the amount of state pension credit payable on` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `under section 159B given the commencing date` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) `with an award in force` TRUE `and an alteration in a component` TRUE `or in benefit income` FALSE `or in a jobseeker's allowance component` FALSE `or in a war pension` FALSE `that affects the computation` TRUE `outside any prescribed exception` FALSE `from the amount before` 50 `to the amount after` 60 EQUALS JUST 60
